  "0.7": {
    "en": [
      "A bonus: Windows 11 light cursors. Configurations, Bonus. It is not part of any profile: one click applies them and one click puts your own cursors back.",
      "A calmer look: the background is always on (it stays still when Windows animations are off or a high-contrast theme is used) and the green glow in the corner is gone.",
      "The start page, System and Settings carry fewer words; System no longer shows power, uptime and type (the saved report still has them).",
      "A button no longer keeps a glow after a mouse click; the keyboard ring still shows when you press Tab.",
      "Apps says why it cannot check an app instead of only \"Can't check\", and the log keeps winget's own answer.",
      "On Optimization, settings that are not for this PC are gathered by reason, and the button is simply \"Apply\" (a window still shows everything first).",
      "Checking for updates when nothing is published yet no longer shows a technical code.",
      "Apps offers to make an installed browser (Brave, Chrome) the one that opens web links: Windows keeps that choice to itself, so the button opens its page and Mesura checks the result when you come back."
